=== Prompt ===
Who is Lara Croft?

=== Response ===
Lara Croft is a fictional character and the protagonist of the Tomb Raider video game series created by British developer Core Design (now known as Crystal Dynamics). She was first introduced in 1996 and has since become one of the most iconic and recognizable video game characters.

Lara Croft is an archaeologist and adventurer known for her intelligence, physical prowess, and determination. She travels the world to find and recover ancient artifacts, often facing dangerous obstacles and enemies along the way. The character is known for her sharp wit, resourcefulness, and ability to overcome seemingly impossible challenges.

In addition to the video games, Lara Croft has been featured in several novels, comics, and television shows. Perhaps most notably, she has been portrayed in three live-action films starring Angelina Jolie, released between 2001 and 2003, which brought her character to a wider audience and helped solidify her status as a pop culture icon.

